secubox-aggregator (0.2.1-1~bookworm1) bookworm; urgency=medium

  * Phase 7 follow-up (#498) — relax hardening for module sudoers :
    - NoNewPrivileges=false (was true). Blocked tightly-scoped sudo
      drops shipped by individual modules (e.g. secubox-crowdsec's
      cscli + nft read-only entries) ; the sudoers entries are the
      real defense in depth.
    - ReadWritePaths += /var/lib/crowdsec (cscli rewrites perms on
      crowdsec.db at every invocation) + /etc/secubox (module config
      writes touched by toolbox/dpi).

